  "name": "gStudy",
  "note": "Two oracles, because two independent things can be wrong: the ANOVA producing the mean squares, and the expected-mean-square algebra turning them into variance components. `meanSquares` comes from statsmodels, which does not know what a G-study is; `components` is the EMS arithmetic on those numbers. `rawComponents` is recorded before truncation so a clamp can be told from a coincidence.",
